.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_GET_EVENT_TIMEOUT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_get_event_timeout
.Nd determine when an SSL object next needs to have events handled
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_get_event_timeout
.Fa "SSL *s"
.Fa "struct timeval *tv"
.Fa "int *is_infinite"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_get_event_timeout
determines when the SSL object next needs to perform internal processing
due to the passage of time.
.Pp
All arguments are required;
.Fa tv
and
.Fa is_infinite
must be non-NULL.
.Pp
Upon the successful return of
.Fn SSL_get_event_timeout ,
one of the following cases applies:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It
The SSL object has events which need to be handled immediately; The
fields of
.Em *tv
are set to 0 and
.Em *is_infinite
is set to 0.
.It
The SSL object has events which need to be handled after some amount of
time (relative to the time at which
.Fn SSL_get_event_timeout
was called).
.Em *tv
is set to the amount of time after which
.Xr SSL_handle_events 3
should be called and
.Em *is_infinite
is set to 0.
.It
There are currently no timer events which require handling in the
future.
The value of
.Em *tv
is unspecified and
.Em *is_infinite
is set to 1.
.El
.Pp
This function is currently applicable only to DTLS and QUIC connection
SSL objects.
If it is called on any other kind of SSL object, it always outputs
infinity.
This is considered a success condition.
.Pp
For DTLS, this function can be used instead of the older
.Xr DTLSv1_get_timeout 3
function.
Note that this function differs from
.Xr DTLSv1_get_timeout 3
in that the case where no timeout is active is considered a success
condition.
.Pp
Note that the value output by a call to
.Fn SSL_get_event_timeout
may change as a result of other calls to the SSL object.
.Pp
Once the timeout expires,
.Xr SSL_handle_events 3
should be called to handle any internal processing which is due; for
more information, see
.Xr SSL_handle_events 3 .
.Pp
Note that
.Fn SSL_get_event_timeout
supersedes the older
.Xr DTLSv1_get_timeout 3
function for all use cases.
.Pp
If the call to
.Fn SSL_get_event_timeout
fails, the values of
.Em *tv
and
.Em *is_infinite
may still be changed and their values become unspecified.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 1 on success and 0 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SSL_handle_events 3 ,
.Xr DTLSv1_get_timeout 3 ,
.Xr ssl 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn SSL_get_event_timeout
function was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
